Q1. What is Automation Testing?

Interview Ready Answer

Automation Testing is a software testing technique in which test
cases are executed automatically using testing tools or scripts
instead of being performed manually by a tester.

It helps execute repetitive test cases quickly, accurately, and
consistently.

Key Points

• Test execution is automated.
• Uses testing tools/scripts.
• Faster than Manual Testing.
• Reduces human errors.
• Best for repetitive testing.

======================================================================

Q2. Why do we need Automation Testing?

Interview Ready Answer

Automation Testing is required to reduce manual effort, execute
repetitive test cases quickly, improve testing accuracy, and support
continuous testing during software development.

Advantages

• Faster execution.
• Reduces human errors.
• Reusable test scripts.
• Higher test coverage.
• Saves time and effort.
• Best suited for Regression Testing.

Real-Life Example

E-commerce Website

Whenever a new feature is added,

↓

Login

↓

Cart

↓

Payment

↓

Order

must be tested again.

Instead of testing manually every time,

Automation Testing executes all test cases automatically.

======================================================================

Q3. Difference between Manual Testing and Automation Testing.

Interview Ready Answer

Manual Testing

• Performed by a human tester.
• Slower execution.
• More prone to human errors.
• Suitable for Exploratory Testing.
• No programming knowledge required.

------------------------------------------------------------

Automation Testing

• Performed using tools/scripts.
• Faster execution.
• More accurate and consistent.
• Best suited for Regression Testing.
• Basic programming knowledge is usually required.

