Q4. What are the different types of Testing?

Interview Ready Answer

Unit Testing

• Tests a single method or function.

Example

calculateSalary()

------------------------------------------------------------

Integration Testing

• Tests communication between multiple modules.

Example

Login

↓

Service

↓

Database

------------------------------------------------------------

Functional Testing

• Verifies whether a feature works according to business
  requirements.

Example

Add to Cart

------------------------------------------------------------

End-to-End (E2E) Testing

• Tests the complete application workflow.

Example

Login

↓

Search Product

↓

Payment

↓

Order Success

------------------------------------------------------------

Performance Testing

• Measures application speed, stability, and scalability.

Example

Testing whether an application can handle thousands of users
simultaneously.

======================================================================

Q5. When should we use Automation Testing?

Interview Ready Answer

Automation Testing should be used for repetitive tasks, Regression
Testing, Smoke Testing, and scenarios where the same test cases are
executed multiple times.

Manual Testing is preferred for Exploratory Testing, Usability
Testing, and situations requiring human judgment.

